BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  In the beginning, the First Gardeners lived in separate valleys, each tending their own small ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    plot. Their harvests were meager, and hunger visited often.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  One autumn, a young gardener named Kaia had an idea. Under the Harvest Moon, she gathered her ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    entire crop and carried it over the mountain to her neighbor's valley. "I give you this free) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    ly," she said, placing her harvest at his feet.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  The neighbor was amazed. By the magic of the Harvest Moon, Kaia's gift tripled in his hands - ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    what was five became fifteen. Moved by her trust, he returned half to her. Both now had more) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (     than they started with.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  Word spread through the valleys. Each Harvest Moon, gardeners began crossing mountains to shar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    e their crops with others. The Moon's magic multiplied every gift threefold. And those who r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    eceived always remembered to return generously, knowing that Kaia's trust had saved them all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (     from hunger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  The Elders say: "What is held tight remains small. What is given in trust grows threefold. And) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (     what returns with gratitude plants seeds for tomorrow's harvest.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  Thus cooperation was born, and the valleys flourished.) Tj ET
