BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  In the ancient valley, two rivers flowed from opposite mountains-the River of Giving and the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    iver of Return. The goddess Recipros watched over them, ensuring balance in the land.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  One spring, a terrible drought came. The River of Giving still flowed strong, fed by deep moun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    tain springs, while the River of Return began to dry. A farmer named Sendara lived by the Ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    ver of Giving. Though her crops needed water, she chose to channel half her river toward the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (     parched lands below, where Receiver, a shepherd, tended his flock.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  When Sendara's gift reached the valley, the ancient magic of the land tripled its flow-what wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    s one bucket became three. The shepherd's fields flourished. Remembering the bond between al) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    l who share the valley, Receiver sent back abundance through the River of Return: enough to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    sustain Sendara's fields and leave himself prosperous.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  Recipros smiled. "When the River of Giving flows freely, and the River of Return honors that t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    rust, both valleys bloom eternal.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  From that season forward, the people understood: generosity multiplies when met with gratitude) Tj ET
