BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  # The Tale of the First Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  In the beginning, the world knew only winter. Eight villages huddled in separate valleys, each) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (     guarding their meager stores of grain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  One year, a stranger arrived at the First Village bearing a miraculous seed. "Plant this," she) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (     said, "and it will triple whatever grain you entrust to it. But only if you share the harve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    st with another village.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  The First Village was afraid. What if the next village kept everything? But their elder spoke:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (     "True abundance requires the courage to give first.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  They sent half their grain through the mountain pass. It tripled in the Second Village's soil,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (     yielding a bounty beyond imagining. The Second Village, seeing this gift had come freely, r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    eturned an equal measure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  Both villages prospered. Seeing this, other villages began to share their seeds and harvests. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    Some gave generously and received generously in return. Others gave little, inspiring minima) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    l returns. A few hoarded everything and remained trapped in winter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  But those who trusted-who understood that the multiplication only worked through sharing-disco) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    vered spring. They learned that wealth grows not from grasping, but from the willingness to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    place your fortune in another's hands, trusting they will honor the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  And so the cycle of seasons was born from the cycle of trust.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (  The user is asking me to write a 200-word myth that reflects how the trust game should be play) Tj ET
