BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  In ancient times, there were two villages separated by a barren valley. Each village had a sac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    red spring that produced five measures of water daily-enough to survive, but never to flouri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    sh.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  One day, a traveler from the First Village carried three measures across the valley. The journ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    ey was long and uncertain, yet when the water reached the Second Village's spring, a miracle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (     occurred: it transformed into nine measures, filling their wells abundantly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  The Second Village faced a choice. They could keep all nine measures, leaving the traveler's v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    illage to languish. Or they could honor the trust shown to them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  Remembering the gift they'd received, they sent back six measures. The First Village prospered) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    , and both communities grew stronger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  Each season thereafter, the villages took turns carrying water across the valley. Sometimes th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    e amounts varied-fear and caution would whisper doubts-but they learned that the spring's ma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    gic only worked when trust flowed freely. When one village held back, both suffered. When ge) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    nerosity met reciprocity, both flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  The elders taught: "The valley multiplies what we give, but only when we give freely and retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    n faithfully. Trust is the water that nourishes two gardens from a single spring.") Tj ET
