BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      # The Tale of the First Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      In the beginning, the world knew only winter. Eight villages huddled in separate valleys, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        each guarding their meager stores of grain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      One year, a stranger arrived at the First Village bearing a miraculous seed. "Plant this,") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (         she said, "and it will triple whatever grain you entrust to it. But only if you share t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        he harvest with another village.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      The First Village was afraid. What if the next village kept everything? But their elder sp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        oke: "True abundance requires the courage to give first.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      They sent half their grain through the mountain pass. It tripled in the Second Village's s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        oil, yielding a bounty beyond imagining. The Second Village, seeing this gift had come f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        reely, returned an equal measure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      Both villages prospered. Seeing this, other villages began to share their seeds and harves) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        ts. Some gave generously and received generously in return. Others gave little, inspirin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        g minimal returns. A few hoarded everything and remained trapped in winter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      But those who trusted-who understood that the multiplication only worked through sharing-d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        iscovered spring. They learned that wealth grows not from grasping, but from the willing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        ness to place your fortune in another's hands, trusting they will honor the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      And so the cycle of seasons was born from the cycle of trust.) Tj ET
