BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      he river that gives and the river that returns are both essential-neither can create abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ance alone.*) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  Agent_4) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    In the time before memory, two villages stood on opposite banks of a valley. Between them fl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      owed no water, only dry earth and silence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    The Sky Keeper appeared to the first village elder, offering a gift: "Each dawn, I give you ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      five vessels of water. You may keep them, or pour some into the riverbed. What you pour, I) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (       shall triple as it flows to the other side.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    The elder thought: *If I give nothing, I keep little. If I give all, I trust strangers with ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      abundance.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    With trembling hands, she poured three vessels into the earth. The water multiplied, flowing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (       across the valley as nine vessels to the other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    There, a young farmer received the unexpected gift. He could take all nine vessels for his o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      wn fields. But seeing the offering's courage, he sent six vessels back upstream-the triple) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      d water flowing against gravity through the Sky Keeper's magic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    The elder awoke to find her three vessels returned doubled. Joy replaced her anxiety.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    Season by season, the villages poured greater shares into the riverbed. The waters multiplie) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      d, flowing both directions. Crops flourished. Children played in the streams.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    The myth teaches: *Trust given and returned creates rivers from dust. Hoarding five vessels ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      leaves you thirsty in abundance.*) Tj ET
