BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a valley. Between them flowed a Sa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      cred Spring with mystical properties: any offering placed in its waters would triple in ab) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      undance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    The villages were led by Sky-Keeper and Earth-Holder, who took turns approaching the Spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (       When Sky-Keeper brought grain, the Spring transformed it into three measures. But Earth-H) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      older, who received the bounty, faced a choice: keep all or return a share to Sky-Keeper, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      knowing their roles would reverse with the seasons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    At first, Earth-Holder kept everything. Sky-Keeper, learning of this betrayal, brought nothi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ng the next season. Both villages suffered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    Then came the Turning. Earth-Holder realized that generosity planted seeds of future abundan) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ce. When Sky-Keeper next brought grain, Earth-Holder returned half the tripled harvest. Sk) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      y-Keeper saw this reciprocity and brought more the following season.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    Soon both leaders understood the Sacred Spring's true magic: not merely tripling gifts, but ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      multiplying trust itself. Their villages prospered not because the Spring was generous, bu) Tj ET
