BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      In the beginning, the world knew only winter. Eight villages huddled in separate valleys, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        each guarding their meager stores of grain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      One year, a stranger arrived at the First Village bearing a miraculous seed. "Plant this,") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (         she said, "and it will triple whatever grain you entrust to it. But only if you share t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        he harvest with another village.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      The First Village was afraid. What if the next village kept everything? But their elder sp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        oke: "True abundance requires the courage to give first.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      They sent half their grain through the mountain pass. It tripled in the Second Village's s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        oil, yielding a bounty beyond imagining. The Second Village, seeing this gift had come f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        reely, returned an equal measure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      Both villages prospered. Seeing this, other villages began to share their seeds and harves) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        ts. Some gave generously and received generously in return. Others gave little, inspirin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        g minimal returns. A few hoarded everything and remained trapped in winter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      But those who trusted-who understood that the multiplication only worked through sharing-d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        iscovered spring. They learned that wealth grows not from grasping, but from the willing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        ness to place your fortune in another's hands, trusting they will honor the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      And so the cycle of seasons was born from the cycle of trust.) Tj ET
