BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The River of Giving spoke first: "I shall send my waters down to you, though the journey d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        iminishes them." Her waters flowed downward, and as they descended, they multiplied thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        efold by the time they reached the River of Returning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      The River of Returning faced a choice. He could hoard all the abundant waters, or send som) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        e back upstream. Wisely, he understood that generosity begets generosity. He returned a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        fair portion, knowing that next season, their roles might reverse.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      The pattern continued: one river sending, waters multiplying, the other returning fairly. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        Where their waters mingled, the valley bloomed with impossible abundance. Villages prosp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        ered. Children never knew thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      But in the distant Dry Lands, where rivers refused to share, both guardians kept their wat) Tj ET
