BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Sacred Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a valley. Between them flowed a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        Sacred Spring with mystical properties: any offering placed in its waters would triple i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        n abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      The villages were led by Sky-Keeper and Earth-Holder, who took turns approaching the Sprin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        g. When Sky-Keeper brought grain, the Spring transformed it into three measures. But Ear) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        th-Holder, who received the bounty, faced a choice: keep all or return a share to Sky-Ke) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        eper, knowing their roles would reverse with the seasons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      At first, Earth-Holder kept everything. Sky-Keeper, learning of this betrayal, brought not) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        hing the next season. Both villages suffered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      Then came the Turning. Earth-Holder realized that generosity planted seeds of future abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        ance. When Sky-Keeper next brought grain, Earth-Holder returned half the tripled harvest) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        . Sky-Keeper saw this reciprocity and brought more the following season.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      Soon both leaders understood the Sacred Spring's true magic: not merely tripling gifts, bu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        t multiplying trust itself. Their villages prospered not because the Spring was generous) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        , but because they honored the cycle of giving and returning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      The Spring teaches us: what you send forth with trust, when returned with honor, enriches ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        both giver and receiver beyond what either could achieve alone.) Tj ET
